WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.800
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:07.180
From stealing candy, to drinking your dad’s
booze or accidentally buying the daily mail,

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:10.400
we’ve all done things we’re not proud
of.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.110
For many of us, if we do something bad, it’s
just a matter of running away or deleting

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:17.630
our browser history and hoping nobody noticed.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:23.100
But throughout human history, many people
have lived with the idea that someone, somewhere,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.990
is keeping a score and when we finally kick
the bucket, we’ll have to account for all

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.220
the bad things that we’ve done.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:35.810
Hell – it immediately conjures up images
of flame-filled caves and red-horned demons

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:37.890
prodding people with forks.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:42.570
But is this what every religion thinks of,
or is it just a part of the Judeo-Christian

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:43.940
tradition.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:47.340
So what do other religions believe?

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:54.630
Today we look at 6 different versions of hell
from around the world.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:01:02.670
Now, if you lived most of your life on frozen
land, crossing the seas under an arctic breeze,

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:07.930
and someone told you there was a way to spend
eternity in a fiery pit then you’d probably

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:10.009
quite like that idea.

00:01:10.009 --> 00:01:16.490
Norse mythology had nine worlds, all connected
by the cosmic ash tree, the Yggdrasil.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:23.010
One of the worlds was Niflheim, the hell of
the Norse, a place of freezing cold darkness.

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:30.080
It was overseen by Loki’s daughter, named
Hel, who also ran Helheim, which was just

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:36.010
for regular dead people, not really bad people
or the great warriors who had died in battle.

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:41.170
Just regular folk that weren’t particularly
liked very much; It mainly consisted of estate

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:43.200
agents and politicians.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.250
Helheim was watched over by a massive eagle
called “Corpse Eater”.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:53.670
One of the other worlds, Muspelheim, consisted
of fire and volcanoes and was ruled by fire

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:54.670
giants.

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:58.909
At the other end of the spectrum was another
of the nine worlds, Asgard, the home of the

00:01:58.909 --> 00:02:00.940
gods, ruled by Odin.

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:07.520
Inside Asgard lies Valhalla, where brave warriors
would go to, if they died in battle.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:13.340
Zoroastrianism is one of the oldest religions
in the world and still has a few hundred thousand

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:20.110
followers in India and Iran, as well as some
religious hipsters – its combination of

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:26.290
cosmogonic dualism and eschatological monotheism
is super retro, you wouldn’t get it.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:29.400
Their Supreme Being is Ahura Mazda.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.670
Which isn’t a Japanese sports car.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:36.160
And Zoroastrianism has a really unique afterlife
belief.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:41.050
Once you die, you must cross the beam-shaped
bridge that splits the world of the living

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:43.280
and the dead.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:45.630
But your crossing is dependent on your behavior.

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:50.920
If you were a good person, then you got a
nice wide bridge and were met by a beautiful

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:55.870
spirit called Daena who led you off to the
House of Song, which sounds like a karaoke

00:02:55.870 --> 00:03:00.290
bar and my personal idea of hell, but each
to their own.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:05.629
However, if you were a naughty person, then
the bridge would be razor thin and the demon

00:03:05.629 --> 00:03:10.410
Vizaresh would push you off and you’d fall
into the House of Lies, a filthy place where

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:16.270
you are always alone, permanently tortured
and fed awful, spoilt food.

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:18.140
So basically an NHS hospital.

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:24.720
The ancient Greeks loved a good bit of mythology
and their gods were like the cast of a psychotic,

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.520
horny soap opera.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:32.239
Hades famously ran the regular underworld
but far beneath, as deep as the heavens were

00:03:32.239 --> 00:03:35.940
high, was the black pit called Tartarus.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:40.519
It was created out of chaos at the same time
as the heavens and the earth and was mainly

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:45.319
used to house things the gods wanted out of
the way, like murderous creatures and Adam

00:03:45.319 --> 00:03:46.650
Sandler movies.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:53.019
But it was also used to punish people who
had really bugged the gods and rather than

00:03:53.019 --> 00:03:58.280
a generic, off-the-shelf punishment for everyone,
there was a unique punishment for each sinner.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:04.190
Sisyphus had to keep rolling a boulder up
a hill for eternity, Tantalus was always hungry

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:09.910
and thirsty and Ixion had to spin around on
a flaming wheel, which actually sounds quite

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:12.030
fun, for a while anyway.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:17.319
Tartarus was also used to imprison many of
the Titans after they tried to overthrow the

00:04:17.319 --> 00:04:18.319
gods.

00:04:18.319 --> 00:04:24.669
Each Titan was guarded by one of the Hecatonchires,
giants with 50 heads and 100 arms.

00:04:24.669 --> 00:04:30.550
Some stories say how the Titans were burnt
and mankind was created out of their fatty

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:35.189
smoke, a bit like how Eve was made created
from Adam’s rib.

00:04:35.189 --> 00:04:40.180
So the moral of the story is that whatever
your religion, we were all created from some

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.210
kind of barbeque.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:47.360
Much like how the Viking’s gods reflected
their surroundings, the mythology of Samoa

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:51.550
is, as you’d expect from a remote island,
very ocean based.

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:57.949
For example, the God of War lived in O le
Fale o le Fe’e, the House of the Octopus,

00:04:57.949 --> 00:04:59.220
since he was a giant Octopus.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:04.619
The entrance to the underworld was found at
Fafa and dead spirits would have to swim west

00:05:04.619 --> 00:05:10.050
along the cluster of islands until they reached
the furthest point on Upolu and threw themselves

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:14.690
from, “the leaping stone”, to swim on
out to the afterworld.

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:21.099
Fafa housed two entrances, Pulotu lead to
the blessed lands and Sa La Fe was the land

00:05:21.099 --> 00:05:22.270
of the bound.

00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:30.050
It was guarded by a giant called Moso who
jumped from Samoa to Fiji and “may Moso

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:34.449
eat you” is still used as an insult to this
day.

00:05:34.449 --> 00:05:36.669
Next we head to Mongolia.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:41.340
The country has a long history of Shamanism,
including special objects and animals and

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:44.080
sacrificial altars called Ovoos.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:49.499
In Mongolian shamanism, dead souls are judged
by Erkil Khan, the prince of the underworld,

00:05:49.499 --> 00:05:53.930
who does some quick mental arithmetic and
counts up all their good deeds versus their

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:54.930
bad ones.

00:05:54.930 --> 00:06:00.460
If the maths goes against them, as maths tends
to do, then they are hurled into Kasyrgan,

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:03.159
a giant cauldron full of bubbling tar.

00:06:03.159 --> 00:06:09.409
But all is not lost, the less they sinned,
the quicker they rise to the top of the cauldron

00:06:09.409 --> 00:06:15.930
and can go free, to take a shower for a few
hundred years as that tar must be bloody difficult

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:16.930
to get off.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:22.520
What’s more, you’re not in it entirely
on your own since anyone in heaven who benefitted

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:28.550
from one of your good deeds can send a spirit
to drag you up slightly quicker by grabbing

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:30.159
you by the hair.

00:06:30.159 --> 00:06:35.559
Just don’t die bald, that’s what I’m
taking from this; Be good and don’t be bald,

00:06:35.559 --> 00:06:37.460
die in a wig if you must.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:42.499
Finally, we come to the most chilled religion
out there, Rastafarianism.

00:06:42.499 --> 00:06:47.539
It was founded in Jamaica in 1930 when Haile
Selassie became emperor of Ethiopia.

00:06:47.539 --> 00:06:54.179
Rastafarianism thinks of Ethiopia as Zion,
which is the birthplace of mankind and so

00:06:54.179 --> 00:06:56.770
is also heaven on earth.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:07:03.389
You can enter the holy land by literal geographical
travel or in a spiritual way, making the emotional

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:06.889
journey before your lazy body actually gets
there.

00:07:06.889 --> 00:07:11.879
Because your body may have slight motivational
issues given the enormous mountain of weed

00:07:11.879 --> 00:07:13.110
you’ve just gone through.

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:16.669
So that’s heaven, what about hell?

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:20.229
Well, hell was actually Jamaica.

00:07:20.229 --> 00:07:24.300
This is because many Africans ended up in
Jamaica due to the slave trade.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:27.429
So understandably it had a lot of negative
connotations.

00:07:27.429 --> 00:07:34.129
Whether it’s freezing caves, pushing giant
rocks up hills or just good old fire and brimstone,

00:07:34.129 --> 00:07:38.830
at one point we’ve all wished that whoever
just stole our parking space should end up

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:39.830
there.

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:44.610
Eternal punishment may seem ridiculous to
some of us or very plausible to others, I

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:48.580
guess it really depends on how many times
you’ve had to watch frozen with your kids.

00:07:48.580 --> 00:08:05.449
Thanks for the view, subscribe for more Thoughty2.

